/**
 * The trained net, base64 little-endian Int16 (see `net.ts` for the layout).
 * 1560 x 32 x 2 -> 1 (board, Ogre and kings' power inputs), QA=16384 QB=4096 SCALE=400.
 *
 * **Adopted 2026-10-02** from the power-aware candidate `sim/nnue-powers/c-lr1.weights.ts`: the
 * 2026-09-17 net fine-tuned on 176,452 positions from 2,280 games under today's rules (a third without
 * powers; the official powers readings otherwise). Against the net it replaces, colour-swapped pairs:
 * ordinary games +89 +/- 22 Elo at depth 3 (800 games) and +80 +/- 64 at 800 ms a move (120 games);
 * kings' powers games +68 +/- 21 at depth 3 (800 games) and +114 +/- 48 at 800 ms (120 games). Most of
 * the gain in ordinary games is on boards with an Ogre, which the old net could not see. The balance
 * lab stays on `linear` by default. See docs/research/ai-powers-2026-10-02.md.
 *
 * Replaced: the Q6 net adopted 2026-09-17 (docs/research/ai-q6-acceptance-2026-09-16.md), board
 * inputs only; its blob is pinned in sim/nnue-powers/current.arm.json.
 */

/** What the blob predicts: the whole evaluation, or a bounded residual on the linear one. */
